  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Energy Access for 100 Communities, through Interface Engineering, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds a feasibility study (Study) to determine the technical, financial and economic viability of building and operating decentralized mini-grids to support energy access for up to one-hundred (100) unelectrified communities in Cte d&apos;Ivoire (Project). The grantee is the Ministre de l&apos;Economie et des Finances of Cte d&apos;Ivoire. The Ministre du Ptrole, de l&apos;nergie et du Dveloppement des nergies Renouvelables is the beneficiary and will implement the Project through its Direction Gnrale de l&apos;Energie. If implemented, the Project could provide energy access for approximately 192,000 individuals. The Study would be competed among U.S. firms on the USTDA website and publicized via Sam.gov and highlighted through USTDA and Power Africa social media and marketing platforms.</narrative>
  </description>
